---
import AdminLayout from '../../layouts/AdminLayout.astro';

// Migrated from design/landing/admin/restaurants.html (~785 lines). Last of
// the 13 design/landing pages migrated to Astro. AdminLayout owns the shared
// Admin shell (topbar + "Admin sections" tabsbar), the `main h1` / `.meta h3`
// body-font override, and the ≤520px `main` padding rule — see
// AdminLayout.astro. Task 24 also extracted the byte-identical
// table/row/button "shape" CSS this page shares with admin/review.html
// (`.table-wrap` outer wrapper, `.table-wrap thead th`, `.row-main`+
// chevron+`.r-name`, `.r-owner`, `.cell-actions`, `.admin-btn` base+hover,
// `.detail-row` shell) into `src/styles/admin.css`, imported once by
// AdminLayout — see that file's frontmatter comment. Everything below is
// page-specific content (the all-restaurants table with search/filter,
// status badges, expandable org/theme/content detail rows) plus the
// page-specific CSS that either has no counterpart on review.html
// (`.search-field`, `.mono`, `.badge-status`+variants, `.audit`,
// `.admin-btn + .admin-btn` sibling margin, `.empty-row`) or whose declared
// values differ from review.html's even though the selector name matches
// (`.count-pill` is neutral-toned here vs. warning there; `.table-wrap
// table`'s min-width is 880px here vs. 720px there — 7 columns vs. 5;
// `.table-wrap tbody td`'s padding is 11px here vs. 12px there; `.meta`'s
// padding is 12px here vs. 14px there; `.detail-inner`'s grid is 3-col here
// vs. 2-col there) — per Task 24's brief those were deliberately NOT merged
// since the split was ambiguous, so they stay page-specific here too.
//
// Transcribed literally (no `.map()` over a data file), matching
// review.astro's precedent: this is a distinct, cross-tenant admin dataset
// (8 restaurants across owners/orgs) with no existing shared shape in
// `src/data/` (the owner-scoped `restaurants.ts` used by the App surface is
// unrelated — a single owner's own restaurants, not a cross-tenant admin
// list).
//
// SEMANTICS: status badges are informational (published=success,
// pending=warning, draft=neutral, flagged/rejected=error) — no destructive
// action lives on this page itself (Edit / Change status are neutral
// tool-buttons); the only cross-link ("Open in review queue →") reuses the
// same neutral `.admin-btn` shape, not a warning/error tone, since it's
// navigation, not a decision.
//
// INTERACTIVITY: the source's inline <script> (row expand/collapse,
// edit/change-status "prototype feedback" text swap, live search/filter) is
// dropped entirely — matches the dead-action/closed-initial-state precedent
// used throughout this migration (review.astro, menu-editor.astro, etc.).
// All 8 `.detail-row`s are ported `hidden`; the `#totalCount` / `#resultNote`
// text nodes keep their literal pre-JS values ("8 total" / "8 of 8 shown");
// `data-toggle`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, `data-edit`, `data-status`,
// `data-search` attributes are all kept verbatim for fidelity even though
// inert (no JS wired) — Edit / Change status buttons and the search input
// are static affordances, consistent with the rest of the migration.
//
// `<main>` keeps the source's `max-w-[1180px] mx-auto` (restaurants.html:409),
// same as review.astro. The two `/admin/review.html` cross-links (rows 3
// "Verde Kitchen"/4 "Tony's Pizzeria"/5 "Green Bowl" detail-actions) are
// rewritten to the clean `/admin/review` route; no other `.html` links or
// dead `#` stubs exist inside this page's `<main>`.
---
<AdminLayout title="Restaurants — Menufic Admin">
